<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 24 December, from 1800 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1800 CE <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon survives a bomb in the rue Saint-Nicaise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Royalist plotters exploded a barrel bomb in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> street as the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a>'s carriage passed, killing several bystanders but missing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. He used the attack to deport Jacobin opponents.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1814 CE <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Ghent ends the War of 1812</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and American negotiators signed a peace treaty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a>, restoring pre-war borders. News travelled slowly, and the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> was fought two weeks later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1851 CE <span class="tih-ago">175 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fire destroys much of the Library of Congress</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A fire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitol</a> destroyed about 35,000 of the Library of Congress's 55,000 books, including around two-thirds of the collection bought from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a> in 1815.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1914 CE <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Christmas Truce begins on the Western Front</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Christmas Eve, soldiers along parts of the front sang carols across the lines. Over the next day many British and German troops met in no man's land, swapped gifts and buried their dead.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1968 CE <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 8 orbits the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frank Borman, Jim Lovell and Bill Anders became the first people to orbit the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>. They photographed 'Earthrise' and read from Genesis in a Christmas Eve broadcast seen by millions.</p></div></li></ol>
